load @term/seed/structure/space/inner-product
  find inner-product-space

# A Hilbert space: an inner-product space that is complete, so every sequence whose terms grow arbitrarily close
# converges to a limit inside the space. Completeness is what lets analysis run: limits, infinite sums, and the spectral
# theory of operators. The state space of a quantum system is a Hilbert space. The form carries the inner-product space;
# completeness is the added axiom.
form hilbert-space
  link space, like inner-product-space
